-- P5-art-49-annex-viii-ix: Article 49 (registration), Annex VIII (the information to be submitted upon registration) and Annex IX (the information on testing in real world conditions).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026 (a plain-text rendering with no legal effect; src:N is its line N; src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:N is the text as enacted).
-- Group: General (Art 113 second paragraph, assumed: keel fork F-113-groups); Annexes VIII and IX take the group of Article 49, which gives them effect (assumed, not ruled).
-- Version: the Omnibus DELETED points 7 and 9 of Annex VIII Section B (consolidated lines 1865 and 1869). Article 49(4)(b) still names "points 8 and 9" of Section B, so as amended it names a point that is gone:
-- the Annex VIII Section B functions and the Article 49(4) function each encode both texts, with a dispatcher on the version in force. The text as enacted applied only until 26 July 2026 and the group applies only
-- from 2 August 2026, so a dispatcher's as-enacted branch can never be reached through the gate (PLAN.md section 5): each as-enacted function is tested directly.
-- Gates. Article 49(1) and (3) and Annex VIII Sections A to C are about one high-risk AI system: they pass the route, placement date and design change to the keel's gate, and Art 111(2) may save the system (NOTHING).
-- Article 49(2) is about a system its provider has concluded is NOT high-risk (Art 6(3)), so Art 111(2), which speaks of high-risk AI systems, is not applied: the date only (fork F-49-2-saving). Article 49(4), 49(5) and Annex IX
-- pass the date only: the restricted section and who may see it do not depend on one system's history, and testing in real world conditions happens before any placing on the market (fork F-49-4-gate).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the text's own yes / no in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md).

§ `Article 49: registration`

DECLARE `Art 49 registrant` IS ONE OF
    `Art 49 the provider`
    `Art 49 the authorised representative`

DECLARE `Art 49 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 49(1) register themselves and their system in the EU database`
    `Art 49(2) register themselves and the AI system in the EU database`
    `Art 49(3) register themselves, select the system and register its use in the EU database`
    `Art 49(4) make the registration in a secure non-public section of the EU database`

DECLARE `Art 49(4) part` IS ONE OF
    `Art 49(4) Annex VIII Section A`
    `Art 49(4) Annex VIII Section B`
    `Art 49(4) Annex VIII Section C`
    `Art 49(4) Annex IX`

§§ `Article 49(1): a high-risk AI system listed in Annex III`

-- "with the exception of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III": an exception, so for point 2 the text's own no (JUST FALSE); a system not listed in Annex III is outside the sentence (NOTHING, a scope limit
-- with no "only"). "Before placing on the market or putting into service": the date on which the system is, or was, placed on the market or put into service is an input shared with the keel's gate; the registration is due by that date,
-- read at the granularity of a day (a registration on that day is in time: fork F-49-before). "the provider or, where applicable, the authorised representative": the registrant is the authorised representative where one applies,
-- else the provider (fork F-49-1-rep: the other reading is that both are bound).
-- src:739 | 1. Before placing on the market or putting into service a high-risk AI system listed in Annex III, with the exception of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III, the provider or, where applicable, the authorised representative shall register themselves and their system in the EU database referred to in Article 71.
@ref Art 49(1) (src:739)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is listed in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 49(1) the registration in the EU database is required` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 49 1)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF NOT `the high-risk AI system is listed in Annex III`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a high-risk AI system listed in Annex III" (a scope limit with no "only")
              ELSE IF `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` EQUALS 2
                   THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the exception of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III"
                   ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:739 | 1. Before placing on the market or putting into service a high-risk AI system listed in Annex III, with the exception of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III, the provider or, where applicable, the authorised representative shall register themselves and their system in the EU database referred to in Article 71.
@ref Art 49(1), who registers (src:739)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is listed in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` IS A NUMBER
      `an authorised representative applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 49 registrant`
`Art 49(1) who must register themselves and their system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 49(1) the registration in the EU database is required` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the high-risk AI system is listed in Annex III` `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `an authorised representative applies`
        THEN JUST `Art 49 the authorised representative`  -- "where applicable, the authorised representative" (fork F-49-1-rep)
        ELSE JUST `Art 49 the provider`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the registration is not required on these facts (the Boolean function above says whether JUST FALSE or NOTHING)

-- src:739 | 1. Before placing on the market or putting into service a high-risk AI system listed in Annex III, with the exception of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 2 of Annex III, the provider or, where applicable, the authorised representative shall register themselves and their system in the EU database referred to in Article 71.
@ref Art 49(1), in time (src:739)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is listed in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` IS A NUMBER
      `the registration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the registration was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 49(1) the registration was made before the placing on the market or the putting into service` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 49 1)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE CONSIDER `Art 49(1) the registration in the EU database is required` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the high-risk AI system is listed in Annex III` `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the registration has been made` AND `the date on which the registration was made` AT MOST `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
                  THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before placing on the market or putting into service" (the date has passed with no registration in time)
                  ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the date of placing on the market has not yet passed, so the duty is not yet breached
         OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no registration is required on these facts

-- The same question put to each bearer: the provider is bound unless an authorised representative applies; the authorised representative is bound where one applies (fork F-49-1-rep). Where no registration is required
-- the answer of the Boolean function above (JUST FALSE for point 2, NOTHING otherwise) is given again.
