§§ `Article 49(2): an AI system the provider has concluded is not high-risk`

-- src:740 | 2. Before placing on the market or putting into service an AI system for which the provider has concluded that it is not high-risk according to Article 6(3), that provider or, where applicable, the authorised representative shall register themselves and that system in the EU database referred to in Article 71.
@ref Art 49(2) (src:740)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the provider has concluded that the AI system is not high-risk according to Article 6(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 49(2) the registration in the EU database is required` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `the provider has concluded that the AI system is not high-risk according to Article 6(3)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an AI system for which the provider has concluded that it is not high-risk according to Article 6(3)" (a scope limit with no "only")

-- src:740 | 2. Before placing on the market or putting into service an AI system for which the provider has concluded that it is not high-risk according to Article 6(3), that provider or, where applicable, the authorised representative shall register themselves and that system in the EU database referred to in Article 71.
