      `the provider has concluded that the AI system is not high-risk according to Article 6(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorised representative applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 49 registrant`
`Art 49(2) who must register themselves and the AI system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 49(2) the registration in the EU database is required` `the date asked` `the provider has concluded that the AI system is not high-risk according to Article 6(3)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `an authorised representative applies`
        THEN JUST `Art 49 the authorised representative`  -- "where applicable, the authorised representative" (fork F-49-1-rep)
        ELSE JUST `Art 49 the provider`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the registration is not required on these facts

